.TH DINIT-SETTINGSD 8 "October 2026" "dinit-settingsd 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
dinit-settingsd \- hostname1, timedate1 and locale1 D-Bus services for dinit systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/libexec/dinit-settingsd
[\fB\-\-read\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-ntp\-service\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Implements the freedesktop.org hostname1, timedate1 and locale1 interfaces so
desktop settings panels can change the hostname, time zone, NTP, RTC mode,
locale and keyboard layout without systemd. It is started on demand by the
system bus and exits after 60 seconds without activity. Changes are
authorized through polkit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-read\-only
Refuse every change with org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.NotSupported.
.TP
.BI \-\-ntp\-service " NAME"
Use only this dinit service for NTP instead of the configured list.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hostname, /etc/machine-info
Static hostname; pretty name, icon, chassis, deployment, location.
.TP
.I /etc/localtime, /etc/adjtime
Time zone and RTC mode (UTC or LOCAL).
.TP
.I /etc/locale.conf
System locale variables.
.TP
.I /etc/rc.conf
KEYMAP (console keymap) and TIMEZONE if present.
.TP
.I /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/00-keyboard.conf
X11 keyboard layout, model, variant and options.
.TP
.I /etc/dinit-settingsd.conf
Optional. ntp-services=chronyd sets the NTP service order (default: chronyd).
NTP is enabled by linking the service into /etc/dinit.d/boot.d and started or stopped with dinitctl.
.SH NOTES
Shell-style files are edited line by line: only the assignment being changed is
rewritten, and the program refuses to touch an assignment it cannot parse
(for example a value spanning several lines).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dinit-settingsctl (1),
.BR dinitctl (8)
